# Backend (`apps/api`)

Extends the core rule and `AGENTS.md`.

- `main.py`: `create_app(settings)` factory. `config.py`: `Settings` (pydantic-settings,
  `ORBIT_*`), read via `get_settings()`. `api/v1/`: versioned routers at `/api/v1`.
- Thin routes with Pydantic request and response models. Return typed models.
- As features land, split schemas, framework-free services, and infrastructure adapters per
  `docs/architecture.md`, but only when a feature needs them.
- Full type hints; Pyright is strict. No unexplained `# pyright: ignore`.
- Explicit exceptions mapped to safe HTTP errors. No swallowed exceptions, and no secrets or
  internals in responses or logs. No hardcoded config or credentials.
- `async def` only when awaiting async I/O.
- After changing routes or exposed models: `pnpm contracts:generate` and include the result in
  the same change.
- Verify in `apps/api`: `uv run ruff check .`, `uv run ruff format --check .`,
  `uv run pyright`, `uv run pytest`.
